From e0395ef6fa634a554c5f6ddc3ebdd4a6c6599921 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:07:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(nix): vendor patchelf repair and retain stable cache
 outputs [daveey]

Problem: main Nix jobs repeatedly fail fetching the patchelf patch with
HTTP 503 or time out while rehydrating its compiler closure (44634702886,
44649483747, 44660246200, 44668661423, 44673995106, 44676428709).
Why: pm tools depend on unreleased patched patchelf, fetched from GitHub.
Its output is not a runtime dependency of those tools, so unrooted store
GC can discard it before saving; immutable primary-key hits then never
update that cache. Upstream availability remains on every run's path.
Root (happened): stable build outputs were not retained at the GC boundary.
Root (not caught): step timing/green streaks did not observe actual fetches.
Recurrence: prior cache-save repair restored upload but not retention.

Vendor the upstream src-only change and share the derivation with a GC root
containing the PM runtime tools, patchelf, Python environment and pnpm deps.
Root before the cache action's post-job GC, report the measured closure,
and reject roots over the existing 5 GiB limit. Do not expand cache quota.
Always summarize substituter copies and HTTPS fetches; warn on a main
primary-key hit that still copies more than ten paths. tee preserves
failures through pipefail, and missing logs still allow failure summaries.

Proof:
- Before implementation, six new behavioral cases failed (missing helpers).
- Final canonical runner: 1541 tests pass across six files.
- All ten warning/budget/count/missing-input mutants killed.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: all 21 checks pass.
- Real nix build .#ci-cache and root_nix_cache.sh succeeded: patched
  patchelf built with only src/patchelf.cc and src/patchelf.h changed;
  rooted closure 3,082,839,480 bytes < 5,368,709,120 bytes.
- Local Nix lacks sandbox namespaces; required PR Nix CI must prove the
  existing sandbox checks. Main two-run warm-cache acceptance follows land.
